CAT = "s6Comms"; SEG = "COM"
Q = [
('A retail communication another member already filed with a favorable FINRA letter, used unchanged, needs:',
 'No new principal approval', ['A new FINRA filing', 'SEC staff approval', 'Each customer\'s written consent'],
 'Rule 2210(b)(1) exempts from principal approval a retail communication that another member filed and FINRA reviewed favorably, if it is not materially altered.'),
('A newly admitted member firm must pre-file certain retail communications with FINRA for:',
 'One year', ['90 days', 'Two years', 'Until its first exam'],
 'Rule 2210(c)(1)(A) requires a new member to file retail communications used in electronic or other public media at least 10 business days before first use for one year from its membership date.'),
('At a firm past its first year of membership, a retail communication promoting one mutual fund, with no rankings, is filed with FINRA:',
 'Within 10 business days after use', ['10 business days before first use', 'Only when FINRA asks to see it', 'Within 90 days after the year end'],
 'Rule 2210(c)(3)(A) has investment company retail communications filed within 10 business days of first use or publication. In a new member\'s first year, or with in-house rankings, it would be filed before use instead.'),
('A fund ad ranks the fund within a category its own sponsor created. The ad must be filed:',
 'Before first use', ['Within 10 days after use', 'Only once a year', 'Never, if accurate'],
 'Rule 2210(c)(2) requires pre-use filing, at least 10 business days ahead, for rankings or comparisons in a category not generally published or created by the fund, its underwriter or an affiliate.'),
('Under SEC Rule 482, a fund ad quoting performance must also show average annual returns for:',
 '1, 5 and 10 years', ['Only the best year', 'The last quarter alone', 'Its first year only'],
 'Rule 482 standardized performance is average annual total return for 1, 5 and 10 years, or the life of the fund if shorter, so a reader cannot be shown only a flattering period.'),
('Under SEC Rule 135a, a generic investment company ad may:',
 'Explain kinds of funds generally', ['Quote one named fund\'s current yield', 'Include a purchase order form', 'Name a fund\'s largest holdings'],
 'Rule 135a covers generic advertising that explains investment companies and their services without promoting a particular fund. Naming one fund\'s yield turns it into fund advertising.'),
('SEC Rule 156 helps decide whether investment company sales literature is:',
 'Misleading', ['Exempt from filing', 'Approved by the SEC', 'Treated as a prospectus'],
 'Rule 156 lists factors, such as omitted context and unwarranted performance claims, for judging whether fund sales literature is materially misleading under the antifraud rules.'),
('Fund sales literature showing returns without standardized performance is deemed misleading under:',
 'Rule 34b-1', ['Rule 10b-10', 'Rule 15c2-12', 'Rule 15c6-1'],
 'Investment Company Act Rule 34b-1 treats sales literature with performance data as misleading unless it also carries the standardized performance Rule 482 requires.'),
('Under SEC Rule 498, a fund using a summary prospectus may:',
 'Post its full prospectus online', ['Skip registering its shares at all', 'Leave its fee table out entirely', 'Send no document at all'],
 'Rule 498 lets a fund deliver a short summary of key facts while the statutory prospectus and other documents are posted online and sent free on request.'),
('Which item must appear in a mutual fund\'s summary prospectus?',
 'Fee table', ['Every portfolio holding', 'Manager\'s salary', 'Audited balance sheet'],
 'Rule 498 requires the summary to give the objective, the fee table, principal strategies and risks, performance, management, purchase and sale details, taxes and intermediary pay. Full holdings are in shareholder reports.'),
('Under Rule 2211, a set of hypothetical variable life illustrations must include a gross return of:',
 '0%', ['3%', '6%', '12%'],
 'Rule 2211 allows hypothetical illustrations at gross rates up to 12%, but one of them must use a 0% gross rate so the customer sees what charges do with no growth.'),
('Rule 2211 caps the gross rate of return in a hypothetical variable life illustration at:',
 '12%', ['8%', '10%', '15%'],
 'Hypothetical returns may run up to and including a 12% gross rate, alongside the required 0% illustration. Higher assumed returns are not allowed.'),
('A retail communication about a deferred variable annuity must not present it as:',
 'A short-term, liquid investment', ['Subject to market risk and fees', 'Issued by an insurance company', 'Sold only with a prospectus'],
 'Rule 2211 bars implying a variable product is short-term or liquid, since surrender charges and tax penalties often apply to early withdrawals.'),
('Under Rule 2212, a fund ranking used in a retail communication must disclose:',
 'Name of the ranking entity', ['Rep\'s pay on each sale', 'Fund\'s holdings that day', 'Sponsor\'s yearly profit'],
 'Rule 2212 requires the ranking entity, the category and number of funds in it, the period and criteria, and other context. Commissions and holdings are not part of the required ranking disclosure.'),
('Under Rule 2213, a bond fund volatility rating may be used in a retail communication only if it is:',
 'Current, with required disclosure', ['Set by the fund\'s own directors', 'Labeled clearly as a risk rating', 'Based on its stock fund peers'],
 'Rule 2213 allows these ratings only when they are current to the latest calendar quarter, come from an independent third party and carry the prescribed disclosure. A volatility rating may not be called a risk rating.'),
('Printed handouts a rep gives to 40 people at a public seminar are generally:',
 'Retail communications', ['Public appearance remarks', 'Personal correspondence', 'Institutional communications'],
 'The talk itself is a public appearance, but written materials used with it and distributed to more than 25 retail investors are retail communications under Rule 2210.'),
('Under Rule 2210, a communication is institutional only if it is distributed to:',
 'Institutional investors only', ['Over 25 people of any kind', 'Existing retail customers', 'Investors in one state'],
 'An institutional communication goes only to institutional investors, such as other firms, banks and large entities. Any retail recipient changes how it is treated.'),
('Under Rule 2210, a rep\'s correspondence to customers must be:',
 'Reviewed by the firm', ['Filed with FINRA first', 'Pre-approved before each use', 'Sent only by postal mail'],
 'Correspondence falls under the firm\'s supervision and review procedures in Rule 3110(b). It needs no principal approval before use and no FINRA filing.'),
('A rep\'s reply in a live online chat forum about funds generally needs:',
 'Review like correspondence', ['Principal approval before posting', 'Filing with FINRA in 10 days', 'SEC staff review'],
 'Rule 2210 exempts posts in online interactive forums from pre-approval, but they must be supervised and reviewed the way correspondence is.'),
('A Rule 482 fund ad must advise investors, before investing, to consider the fund\'s:',
 'Objectives, risks and expenses', ['Next-year price target', 'Manager\'s personal trading record', 'Ranking among bank CDs'],
 'Rule 482 ads must tell investors to consider objectives, risks, charges and expenses carefully and explain where to get a prospectus with that information.'),
('Ads for a 529 college savings plan fall under which MSRB rule?',
 'G-21', ['G-37', 'G-27', 'G-15'],
 'MSRB Rule G-21 governs advertising of municipal securities, including municipal fund securities like 529 plans. G-27 is supervision and G-15 covers confirmations.'),
('Under Rule 3170, a firm may have to tape-record its reps\' calls when many of them:',
 'Came from disciplined firms', ['Work from their home offices', 'Sell variable annuities', 'Are newly registered'],
 'Rule 3170 makes a firm a taping firm when a set share of its registered persons were recently with firms expelled or with revoked registrations, to protect investors from abusive sales.'),
('An ad for a retail money market fund must warn the reader that:',
 'They could lose money', ['Deposits are FDIC insured', 'The yield is fixed', 'Shares are sold only yearly'],
 'Rule 482 requires money market fund ads to state that an investor could lose money and that the fund is not insured or guaranteed by the FDIC or any government agency.'),
('Retail communications about investment products must give a fair, balanced treatment of:',
 'Risks and possible benefits', ['Only its best past years', 'The rep\'s own past track record', 'Rival firms\' fees and sales charges'],
 'Rule 2210(d)(1) requires communications to be fair and balanced, so benefits may not be stressed while risks are left out or buried.'),
]
